{#- ── US Prophet board CARDS (docs/TIER_PREVIEW_PATTERN.md) ─────────────────────
   Extracted verbatim from the `.nbgrid` loop that used to live inline in
   dashboard.html.j2 (the priority/legacy heading + Prophet card block,
   operator-ratified 2026-07-21 flagship redesign). ONE source for both
   consumers so the free shell and the paid payload can never drift apart:
     · the shell {% with %}-binds these same param names and {% include %}s
       this file at the .nbgrid loop's original location (dashboard.html.j2);
     · scripts/build_site.py._write_us_payload renders it directly via
       env.get_template("_us_board_cards.html.j2").render(...) for the LOCKED
       remainder that ships in site/premiumdata/us_stocks.json.
   Self-contained by the same convention every other extracted partial here
   follows (_us_act_now_board.html.j2, _etf_board_rows.html.j2): its own `pv`
   import and its own copies of the pure-constant label dictionaries the
   original loop read from dashboard.html.j2's outer scope. Carries NO tier
   logic itself — the split happens before this partial is ever called.

   Params:
     items        — the (already-grouped, heading-sentinel-bearing) list a
                     `_render_list` construction produces — see
                     dashboard.html.j2:15837-15895 (legacy lane path) and
                     :15966-15990 (priority stage_hd path), or
                     scripts/build_site.py::_us_board_group_items for the
                     Python-side equivalent used on the locked remainder.
     sg_any       — bool: does ANY row in the FULL board carry `stage`
                     (dashboard.html.j2 `_sg.any` / build_site `sg_any`).
     bs_adj       — bool: W-L1 board-state publish-together fence
                     (dashboard.html.j2 `_bs_adj`).
     xu_allfeat   — bool: every featured row's extension check unmeasured
                     (dashboard.html.j2 `_xu_allfeat`).
     trg_map      — dict ticker -> top_setups row, for the fresh-trigger chip
                     (dashboard.html.j2 `_trg_map`).
     rw_en, rw_zh — the runway-leg coverage receipt sentence appended to the
                     Priority tooltip, or '' when the leg is scored
                     (dashboard.html.j2 `_rw_en`/`_rw_zh`, M1). Board-level,
                     not row-derived, so it is identical on both sides of the
                     wall — computed once and passed through rather than
                     recomputed per card.
-#}
{% import "_prophet_card.html.j2" as pv %}
{%- set _pri_en = ' Higher Priority means the setup is more ready today, not more likely to win.' -%}
{%- set _pri_zh = ' 优先级越高，表示今天越接近可操作，并不代表更容易获胜。' -%}
{%- set _stage_en  = {'live':'Live now','setting_up':'Setting up','ran':'Ran — don’t chase','basing':'Basing','blocked':'Blocked'} -%}
{%- set _stage_zh  = {'live':'现在可操作','setting_up':'形成中','ran':'已启动 — 勿追','basing':'筑底中','blocked':'受阻'} -%}
{%- set _stage_sub_en = {'live':'entry window is open','setting_up':'not there yet — get ready','ran':'the move already started','basing':'no entry signal yet — watch, don’t chase','blocked':'stand aside for now'} -%}
{%- set _stage_sub_zh = {'live':'入场窗口已打开','setting_up':'尚未触发 — 做好准备','ran':'行情已经启动','basing':'尚无入场信号 — 观察，勿追高','blocked':'暂时观望'} -%}
{%- set _stage_tip_en = {
     'live':'The entry window is open now.' ~ _pri_en,
     'setting_up':'The setup is taking shape, but the signals do not agree yet. Get ready; there is nothing to do now.' ~ _pri_en,
     'ran':'The move has already started and the original entry has passed. Wait for a new setup.' ~ _pri_en,
     'basing':'These stocks may be building a low, but no entry has fired. Watch them; do not chase.' ~ _pri_en,
     'blocked':'The trend or entry is not healthy enough. Stand aside for now.' ~ _pri_en } -%}
{%- set _stage_tip_zh = {
     'live':'入场窗口现在已经打开。' ~ _pri_zh,
     'setting_up':'形态正在形成，但信号尚未一致。做好准备，现在无需操作。' ~ _pri_zh,
     'ran':'行情已经启动，原有入场窗口已过。等待下一次机会。' ~ _pri_zh,
     'basing':'这些股票可能正在筑底，但尚无入场信号。观察，勿追高。' ~ _pri_zh,
     'blocked':'趋势或入场条件还不够健康。暂时观望。' ~ _pri_zh } -%}
{%- set _lane_labels_en = {'bottoming':'Bottoming','continuation':'Continuation','trend':'Trend','recovery':'Recovery','watch':'Watch'} -%}
{%- set _lane_labels_zh = {'bottoming':'筑底','continuation':'延续','trend':'趋势','recovery':'复苏','watch':'观察'} -%}
      {% for n in items %}
        {# heading sentinel — two idioms, one loop: `stage_hd` is the priority-order
           path (G0.1), `lane` is the legacy lane partition an old artifact still gets. #}
        {% if n.get('_heading') and n.get('stage_hd') %}
        {% set _sk = n.stage_hd %}
        <div class="nb-stage-hd sg-{{ _sk }}" data-stage="{{ _sk }}" data-sm-heading="1" data-tip-en="{{ _stage_tip_en[_sk] }}" data-tip-zh="{{ _stage_tip_zh[_sk] }}">
          <span class="sh-l"><span class="l-en">{{ _stage_en[_sk] }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _stage_zh[_sk] }}</span></span>
          <span class="sh-n">{{ n.count }}</span>
          <span class="sh-s"><span class="l-en">{{ _stage_sub_en[_sk] }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _stage_sub_zh[_sk] }}</span></span>
        </div>
        {% elif n.get('_heading') %}
        {# `data-lane` is the legacy path's join key, mirroring `data-stage` above:
           on a gated board the shell and the tier payload each render their own
           heading for a group that spans both sides of the wall, and the page's
           hydrate() merges them by this attribute (dashboard.html.j2). Without it
           the lane path can only fall back to appending, which is what drew the
           heading twice. Display is unchanged — the CSS keys on the class. #}
        <div class="nb-lane-hd" data-lane="{{ n.lane }}" data-sm-heading="1">
          <span class="l-en">{{ _lane_labels_en.get(n.lane, n.lane) }} · {{ n.count }}</span>
          <span class="l-zh">{{ _lane_labels_zh.get(n.lane, n.lane) }} · {{ n.count }}</span>
        </div>
        {% else %}
        {# ═══ PROPHET CARD (flagship redesign, operator-ratified 2026-07-21) ═══
           The old multi-chip standout card is retired; every prior at-rest disclosure
           survives DEMOTED, not deleted: verdict sentence + entry headline → verb-chip
           tooltip; cautions / sector-stance / anti-chase / extension / earnings-window /
           base-broken → the single ⚠N popover; Edge %ile meaning → Edge tooltip; tier/sig
           badge + cycle detail → stock.html analyzer (one click). Builder fields consumed
           unchanged — display-tier change only; lane grouping (R7) untouched. #}
        {% set c = n.conviction %}
        {% set es = n.entry_signal %}
        {% set _is_triage = (c and c.get('score_edge') is not none and c.score_edge >= 80) and (es and es.get('status') in ['buy_now','partial']) %}
        {% set _st = es.status if es else none %}
        {% set _verb = 'buy' if _st in ('buy_now','partial')
                 else ('near' if _st in ('buy_soon','await_confluence')
                 else ('hold' if _st in ('hold','topping')
                 else ('avoid' if _st in ('exit','avoid')
                 else ('wait' if _st
                 else ('near' if n.dir == 'up' else ('avoid' if n.dir == 'down' else 'wait')))))) %}
        {% set _stage = {'bottoming':1,'recovery':2,'continuation':3,'trend':4}.get(n.get('lane') or '', 0) %}
        {% set _vs = c.vol_squeeze if c else none %}
        {% set _vs_fired = _vs and _vs.state in ['FIRED_UP','EXPANSION'] %}
        {% set _entry_ok = not (es and es.get('status') in ['extended','topping','exit','avoid','blocked']) %}
        {% set _fl = namespace(rows=[]) %}
        {% if c %}{% for cau in (c.cautions or []) %}{% if cau != 'accounting watch' %}{% set _z = c.cautions_zh[loop.index0] if (c.cautions_zh and c.cautions_zh|length > loop.index0) else cau %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [(cau, _z)] %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
        {% if (_vs_fired or n.get('alpha_entry') == 'extended') and _entry_ok %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [("Already moving. Don't chase above the buy zone.", '已在异动。不要在买区上方追高。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('ext_z') is not none and n.ext_z > 2.0 %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Stretched unusually far above its trend line, so chasing is risky.', '远高于趋势线，追高风险较大。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('antichase_shadow_blocked') %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Parabolic tail. Treat any entry here as a chase.', '处于抛物线尾部。此处入场应视同追高。')] %}{% endif %}
        {# ── COPY FENCE: the two rows ABOVE are the ext_z anti-chase read (px/SMA200
             z-scored).  The "Blow-off risk" chip built in the marks row BELOW is a
             SEPARATE, separately-measured construction (12-session ROC at its own
             trailing p99 inside a burst-mover uptrend, engine/roc_blowoff.py), and the
             battery's PM4 redundancy read puts max |rho| between them at 0.43 — so both
             can legitimately fire on one card.  Because they can co-render, the blow-off
             chip must NEVER use the bare word "Extended": that word already belongs to
             the ext_z family here and in engine/stock_score.py's conviction verdict, and
             two different measurements wearing one word is how a card starts arguing with
             itself.  "Blow-off risk" / 冲顶风险 is the label; the numbers in its hover are
             ITS OWN measured rates, never the ext_z ones. #}
        {% set _es_chip = n.get('earnings_soon') %}
        {% if _es_chip and _es_chip.get('days_to') is not none %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [(_es_chip.get('chip_en') or ('Earnings in ' ~ _es_chip.days_to ~ 'd'), _es_chip.get('chip_zh') or ('财报还有' ~ _es_chip.days_to ~ '天'))] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('sector_stance') and n.sector_stance in ('Reduce','Cautious') %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Sector stance is ' ~ n.sector_stance|lower ~ '. This is a single-stock trigger, not a sector call.', '板块态度为' ~ (n.sector_stance_zh or n.sector_stance) ~ '。个股信号，非板块判断。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('hold') and n.hold.get('state') == 'broken' %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Base broken: price hit the level that voids the thesis.', '筑底破位：价格已触及使论点失效的水平。')] %}{% endif %}
        {# OEU M-PRO: display-tier options context, folded into the SAME ⚠ popover as every
           other caution (no new chip, no layout change). Rows are pre-derived (en, zh) pairs
           attached by build_site._attach_board_display_chips via lib/options_context.py; the
           fence lives there — nothing here touches verb, stage, zone or edge. Names without
           options coverage carry no key and the card renders exactly as before. #}
        {% for _o in (n.get('options_flags') or []) %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [(_o[0], _o[1])] %}{% endfor %}
        {# ── MARKS ROW (priority engine): four categorically different facts in
             descending weight — rank, recency, setup shape, theme. Built only on the
             priority path; on the legacy path the lane IS the heading, so no chip.
             `featured` supersedes the triage ring: one accent per card. #}
        {% set _feat = sg_any and n.get('featured') %}
        {% set _mk = namespace(rows=[]) %}
        {% if sg_any %}
          {# m5: the featured edge gate is "residual alpha at or above zero" — an ABSOLUTE
             floor, not a rank against the rest of the board (engine/us_board_rank.py
             ranking_block, featured_requirements). "Above the board's midpoint" described
             a cross-sectional test the engine never runs, and on a weak board it would
             have promised the opposite of what the gate actually does. #}
          {# Blow-off risk FIRST: it is the only risk read in this row, and a marks row
             wraps — buried behind a theme name it would be the one chip a reader misses.
             Display-only (engine/us_board_rank.ZERO_SCORE_AUTHORITY carries blowoff_risk);
             see the copy fence above for why it never says "Extended". #}
          {% if (n.get('blowoff') or {}).get('blowoff_risk') %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'blow','en':'Blow-off risk','zh':'冲顶风险',
            'tip_en':'12-day move at its own 1-in-100 extreme near highs. Historically within 5 sessions of a local top 24% of the time (vs 19% base); next-21-session drawdowns ran ~2.5pp deeper. 3 of 4 such extremes are still not the top — risk context, not a sell signal.',
            'tip_zh':'12日涨幅处于自身历史百分之一的极值，且贴近高点。历史上此类情形有24%在5个交易日内就是局部顶部（基准19%）；其后21个交易日的回撤中位数深约2.5个百分点。四次中仍有三次并非顶部——这是风险背景，不是卖出信号。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {# THE EXTENSION CLAUSE IS CONDITIONAL, because the check it describes does not
             always run.  Until 2026-08-08 a row with no extension reading was VETOED
             out of featured, so "price is not extended" was true of every row that
             carried this chip.  ANTICIPATION v1 replaced that veto with a disclosure
             (engine/us_board_rank.py — an outage published a featured lane of 0 of 69),
             so a featured row may now carry `ext_unknown: true` — and on that row the
             old sentence is a verification the board never performed, asserted in the
             one place a reader goes to find out what the gate tested.  Plain-word
             printed null instead (DESIGN_DOCTRINE Law 5): the absence is stated on the
             same tier as the claim it replaces, in the reader's own words, no slug.

             THIS TIP IS STILL NOT RENDERED — `_prophet_card.html.j2` carries
             `_MK_NOTIP = ('feat', 'new')` (operator 2026-08-05 — the featured explainer
             covered neighbouring cards), so the string below is built and dropped on
             the floor. It is kept correct rather than deleted because the suppression
             is a layout decision that can be revisited, and a string that comes back
             wrong is worse than one that comes back right. The visible carrier the
             disclosure needs is the `nck` chip immediately below, NOT this tip. #}
          {% set _xu = n.get('ext_unknown') %}
          {% if _feat %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'feat','en':'★ Featured','zh':'★ 精选',
            'tip_en':'One of today’s featured names: the signal is fresh, the entry is open and stock strength is positive' ~ ('. We could not check how far it has already run tonight.' if _xu else ', with room left to run.') ~ ' Up to 12 names can be featured, with no more than four per sector.',
            'tip_zh':'今日精选之一：信号新鲜、入场窗口已打开，个股强度为正' ~ ('。今晚无法检查它已经涨了多远。' if _xu else '，仍有上行空间。') ~ '精选区最多12只，每个板块不超过4只。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {# ── THE PER-ROW CARRIER (ANTICIPATION v1 · the design call #4976 deferred).
               ★ Featured is a claim about which checks this name passed; on an
               `ext_unknown` row one of those checks never ran, and until now the only
               place that said so was the board footnote's aggregate count. The reader
               could learn that N of the picks were unmeasured but never WHICH — so the
               mark goes on the card, immediately after the claim it qualifies. Adjacency
               is the whole point: "★ Featured · Extended? Not checked" is one sentence.

               FEATURED ROWS ONLY, deliberately, though the engine stamps `ext_unknown`
               on every row. The extension reading feeds the featured gate; on a Wait or
               Blocked card nothing on the card leans on it, so the mark would answer no
               question the reader is asking (doctrine Law 1) while spending a slot in a
               row whose median card shows one chip. It qualifies a claim, so it renders
               only where the claim is.

               SUPPRESSED WHEN THE WHOLE SHELF IS UNKNOWN — see `xu_allfeat` above.

               COPY: "Extended?" is the board's own word for this measurement (the
               footnote below says "price not extended"), and the question mark does the
               work no adjective can — it says the matter is open, so the chip can be
               neither read as "this name IS extended" nor as an all-clear. Question-as-
               label is ratified house case law (DESIGN_DOCTRINE §7, census-distilled
               patterns). It must NOT borrow the blow-off chip's vocabulary or hue: that
               is a different measurement with its own rates, and the copy fence above
               keeps the two apart in both directions. #}
          {% if _feat and _xu and not xu_allfeat %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'nck','en':'Extended? Not checked','zh':'涨过头？未检查',
            'tip_en':'One of the checks behind ★ Featured did not run for this name tonight: whether price has already run too far to be worth buying here. No reading came through, so nothing was scored — an absence, not a finding that it has. Everything else the shelf tests was scored and passed: fresh signal, entry window open, edge above zero. Tonight, judge the run-up off the chart above yourself.',
            'tip_zh':'「★ 精选」背后有一项检查今晚没能对这只股票完成：价格是不是已经涨过头、现在买不划算。今晚没取到读数，这一条就没参与判定 —— 是「没查」，不是「查出来涨过头了」。其余几项都已判定并通过：信号新鲜、入场窗口已打开、优势为正。今晚这一项，请自己看上面的走势图判断。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {% if n.get('new') %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'new','en':'New','zh':'新',
            'tip_en':'This signal fired in tonight’s run — the name was not on the board yesterday.',
            'tip_zh':'该信号在今晚这一轮才触发 — 昨天不在榜上。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {# W-L1 `Adjusted` (spec §2 C, §4.3, §6.4) — the receipt of a name that MOVED when
             the overnight pass countersigned last evening's board. Sits with `New` because
             both are recency-class facts ("what changed since you last looked"), ahead of
             setup shape and theme. It is the quietest chip in the row by design and by hue.
             `bs_adj` is the publish-together fence: the mark cannot render unless the
             receipt line it belongs to rendered, so a reader never meets a per-card delta
             with no line explaining what the delta is against. #}
          {% if bs_adj and n.get('adjusted') %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'adj','en':'Adjusted','zh':'已调整',
            'tip_en':'The overnight pass changed something on this name after last evening’s board — most often the entry range or where it sits in the order. The card already shows the updated numbers.',
            'tip_zh':'隔夜复核后，这只股票有变动 —— 多为入场区间或排序位置。卡片上显示的已是更新后的数值。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {% if n.get('theme_confirmed') %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'warm','en':'Theme just turned','zh':'主题刚转向',
            'tip_en':'The stock’s own signal is older, but the basket it belongs to only just turned up. Context for why it may keep working — never a reason to chase.',
            'tip_zh':'个股信号本身较早，但其所属篮子刚刚转强。这解释了它为何可能延续 — 但绝不是追高的理由。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {# The `watch` lane is deliberately NOT chipped here.  Every other lane value
             names the SHAPE of the setup; `watch` names its TIMING — and timing is now
             the stage bucket's job.  Printed as a chip it put two stances on one card:
             a Live-now featured pick reading "★ Featured · Watch". #}
          {% if n.get('lane') and n.lane != 'watch' %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'lane',
            'en':_lane_labels_en.get(n.lane, n.lane), 'zh':_lane_labels_zh.get(n.lane, n.lane),
            'tip_en':'The shape of the setup: bottoming = turning up off a base · continuation = an existing uptrend resuming · trend / recovery = further along. It groups risk, it does not rank the name.',
            'tip_zh':'形态类型：筑底＝自底部转强 · 延续＝原有上升趋势重启 · 趋势／复苏＝走得更远。它用于摆放风险，不决定排名。'}] %}{% endif %}
          {% if n.get('theme') and n.theme.get('name') %}{% set _mk.rows = _mk.rows + [{'k':'theme',
            'en':n.theme.name, 'zh':(n.theme.get('name_zh') or n.theme.name),
            'tip_en':'This stock belongs to a theme that is strengthening. Use it to understand the story; it does not change this card’s Priority.',
            'tip_zh':'该股属于正在转强的主题。可用来理解背景，但不会改变卡片的优先级。'}] %}{% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        {# ── Priority score in the Edge slot (CN cn_prophet_v2 precedent, china.html.j2).
             Rows without prophet.score keep today's conviction-percentile "Edge" display
             exactly as-is — the label, the value and the tooltip all fall back together,
             so a mixed artifact never shows a Priority label over an Edge number. #}
        {% set _prs = (n.get('prophet') or {}).get('score') %}
        {% set _prs = _prs if (_prs is number) else none %}
        {# `none` on the legacy path so an old artifact renders byte-identically;
           `[]` on the priority path so even an unmarked card reserves its slot and the
           tracker/zone rows stay aligned across a grid row. #}
        {% set _mk_slot = _mk.rows if sg_any else none %}
        {% set _bz = es.buy_zone if es else none %}
        {% set _zk = ('readd' if _verb == 'hold' else ('active' if _verb in ('buy','near') else 'muted')) if (_bz and _bz.high is not none) else ('confirm' if _verb in ('wait','near') else 'none') %}
        {# ⚡ fresh-trigger chip: kind from the setups row's own signal tier (T3 = imminent,
           else fired). Tips are plain strings (attribute-safe — no t() in attrs). The verb
           stays the ruling stance; the tip says so for the Wait+⚡ case. #}
        {% set _tsr = trg_map.get(n.ticker) %}
        {% set _tsg = (_tsr.get('signal') or {}) if _tsr else {} %}
        {% set _trg_kind = ('imminent' if _tsg.get('tier_cascade') == 'T3' else 'fired') if _tsr else none %}
        {% set _trg_prov = ' Provisional: projected off an incomplete bar — about 1 in 10 of these vanish when the bar completes.' if (_trg_kind == 'imminent' and _tsg.get('provisional')) else '' %}
        {% set _trg_prov_zh = '（暂定：基于未完成的K线推算 — 约十分之一会在K线完成后消失。）' if (_trg_kind == 'imminent' and _tsg.get('provisional')) else '' %}
        {% set _trg_tip_en = ('Fresh entry trigger — it fired in the last few days and momentum is still building. A conviction card plus a fresh trigger is the strongest read on this board — but the main chip still rules: if this card says Wait, price has already run past the zone; don\'t chase.') if _trg_kind == 'fired' else ('Entry trigger is close — it should fire within the next day or two.' ~ _trg_prov ~ ' The main chip still rules the stance.') %}
        {% set _trg_tip_zh = ('新的入场触发 — 最近几天刚刚触发，动量还在往上走。信念卡片加上新触发，是本板最强的组合 — 但主标签仍然是最终判断：如果卡片写的是「等待」，说明价格已经冲过买点区，不要追。') if _trg_kind == 'fired' else ('入场触发快到了 — 预计一两天内触发。' ~ _trg_prov_zh ~ '主标签仍然是最终判断。') %}
        {#- ── NO DATE IN THE ZONE ROW (2026-08-26, PR-2 of the US permanence program).
             The `date` slot below used to carry `(n.signal or {}).get('asof')`, which put
             a bare date immediately after the buy-zone numbers — and a date pinned against
             numbers reads as the vintage OF those numbers. It is not. Two measurements,
             two clocks, and the shipped artifacts settle which is which:

               · buy_zone is recomputed EVERY session. Comparing the 2026-08-24 board
                 (be061c6d49e9) against the 2026-08-25 board, 101 of 101 common tickers
                 carrying a zone had `low`/`high` MOVE overnight; zero held still.
               · signal.asof is a 3-session bucket clock and is BOARD-WIDE, not per-card:
                 on the 2026-08-25 board all 133 carded rows (buy + watch + leaders +
                 laggards) read the identical `2026-08-21`.

             So the chip printed ONE board constant, 133 times, against numbers four days
             newer than it — and on 2026-08-26 it was read off the board as proof the board
             was five days stale. It was not: `as_of` had advanced nightly throughout.

             Two doctrine rules land on the same answer (DESIGN_DOCTRINE Law 4): "one as-of
             stamp per panel", and "no per-row repetition of a constant — a constant belongs
             in the footer, once". Nothing per-card is lost by removing it, because nothing
             per-card was ever in it. The board's real vintage is now stated ONCE, in plain
             words, on the page header (#stocks-header .stk-status, dashboard.html.j2),
             whose Tier-2 hover also carries this signal-bucket date — at board level,
             where it is true.

             DO NOT restore a date here. If a future artifact ever makes signal.asof
             genuinely per-card, it still would not be the ZONE's vintage, and it would
             need its own labelled slot rather than this bare one. `date` is kept as an
             explicit `none` rather than a deleted key so the slot reads as a decision
             rather than an oversight. The shared macro keeps full `date` support for
             _us_prophet_plan_cards.html.j2, whose dates ARE per-plan and honest. -#}
